                              [--statement-rev STATEMENT_REV] --tip TIP

Count corrections to round-32 C2 self-assessment/evidence mismatches. The
counter grades the SCORECARD claim as it was written at --statement-rev, then
verifies its append-only correction in the evaluated --tip. It reads only Git
blobs and never changes the repository.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --repo REPO           lane Git repository
  --statement-rev STATEMENT_REV
                        full commit that wrote the r32 C2 row
  --tip TIP             full commit whose correction is evaluated
usage: round33-gate-receipts.py [-h] {capture,audit} ...

Capture and audit complete receipts for the round-32 registry gate. Capture
runs the gate code from a pinned lane revision against that revision and three
deterministic, disposable Git fixtures. Fixture Git writes stay under a
temporary directory. Audit reads only committed receipt blobs and replays each
case from its pinned source revision; the lane repository is never mutated.

positional arguments:
  {capture,audit}
    capture        run the pinned gate and three isolated controls
    audit          re-run and compare the four committed receipts

options:
